    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "b61a2b2c-759e-368d-993f-a39465ae64be",
                "word": "mandamus",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e1638b42-5636-4366-acfe-1bb39a9d0ab5",
                        "entry_id": "b61a2b2c-759e-368d-993f-a39465ae64be",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mandamuses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7b11e1d5-2ea7-3885-b2fb-44a719510b84",
                        "entry_id": "b61a2b2c-759e-368d-993f-a39465ae64be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A common law prerogative writ that compels a court or government officer to perform mandatory or purely ministerial duties correctly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c69aca6-c3e4-421f-b5fc-958ea82e4c48",
                                "sense_id": "7b11e1d5-2ea7-3885-b2fb-44a719510b84",
                                "text": "I admit to all my learned friends that a Mandamus does not issue where there is another course of proceeding by which the thing can be effected; but I again state to your Lordships, that if in this case a Mandamus must not issue, there is no other proceeding that can be adopted."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5bbc1b4-0db7-4572-898d-00a1d5854099",
                                "sense_id": "7b11e1d5-2ea7-3885-b2fb-44a719510b84",
                                "text": "And then it was moved that the court would grant a mandamus to the delegates to admit the bishop's allegations: and it was compared to the cases where they grant mandamuses to compel the granting of probates of wills or letters of administration."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "473aafda-00aa-4a18-93e2-a95f983c1b76",
                                "sense_id": "7b11e1d5-2ea7-3885-b2fb-44a719510b84",
                                "text": "A mandamus is a writ commanding the execution of an act, where otherwise justice would be obstructed, or the king's charter neglected, issuing regularly only in cases relating to the public and the government; and is therefore termed […] a prerogative writ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "41321756-9cd2-4e2b-9fcc-1659434b2c2d",
                                "sense_id": "7b11e1d5-2ea7-3885-b2fb-44a719510b84",
                                "text": "The lord is compellable by mandamus to admit the surrenderee, that is, the person to whose use the surrender is made."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
